Open edX apps/MFE domains:

- Production apps/MFE: `https://apps.courses.networked.co` or the production configured apps host
- QA apps/MFE: `https://apps.courses.qa.networked.co` or the QA configured apps host
- Lab apps/MFE: `https://apps.lms.lab.networked.co` or lab-specific apps host
- Local mapped apps/MFE: `http://apps.local.openedx.io`

### Backend Selection Rule

Open edX Networked login code chooses backend by request host:

- host contains `lab` -> `https://backend.lab.networked.co`
- host contains `qa` or `local` -> `https://backend.qa.networked.co`
- otherwise -> `https://backend.networked.co`

So when testing with `local.openedx.io`, the Open edX login bridge can call QA backend unless code/config overrides it.

### Common API URLs

Open edX APIs used during setup/integration:

- CSRF: `/csrf/api/v1/token`
- Open edX registration: `/api/user/v2/account/registration/`
- Open edX login session: `/api/user/v2/account/login_session/`
- Public course list: `/api/courses/v1/courses/`
- Public course detail: `/api/courses/v1/courses/<course_id>`
- Networked course list: `/api/learner_home/networked/courses/`
- Networked course detail: `/api/learner_home/networked/course-detail/<course_id>/`
- Course outline: `/api/course_home/outline/<course_id>`
- Gradebook: `/api/grades/v1/gradebook/<course_id>/`
- Gradebook grading info: `/api/grades/v1/gradebook/<course_id>/grading-info`
- Course grading policy: `/api/grades/v1/policy/courses/<course_id>/`

Networked backend APIs used by Open edX:

- Login data: `/api/v1/auth/openedx-login/data?tokenId=<token>&communityId=<community_id>`
- Header/community metadata: `/api/v1/global/open-edx/header-meta`
- Admin/staff emails: `/api/v1/global/open-edx/<community_id>/admin-staff-emails`

## Full Flow

1. Change code locally.
2. Commit and push to GitHub.
3. SSH into the target server.
4. Pull latest code on server.
5. Remove old local Docker images if needed.
6. Build Tutor images.
7. Tag images for the target environment.
8. Push images to registry.
9. Delete Open edX pods in that environment.
10. Kubernetes recreates pods and pulls the new images.
11. Test LMS, CMS/Studio, Networked redirect, course authoring, learning, and grading.

## Local Git Push

```bash
git status
git add <files>
git commit -m "<message>"
git push origin <branch>
```

Do not push secrets, `.env`, private keys, Tutor env secrets, or production credentials.

## Server Git Pull

```bash
cd <edx-platform-repo>
git fetch origin
git checkout <branch-or-tag>
git pull --ff-only
git status
```

Use the correct branch/tag:

- Lab: lab/dev branch or commit.
- QA: QA branch or commit.
- Production: reviewed production release tag/commit.

If server has local changes, stop and check before pulling.

## Remove Old Images

```bash
docker images | grep -E "openedx|mfe"
docker image prune -f
docker rmi <old-image-tag-or-id>
```

Only remove old Open edX/MFE images. Do not delete database or volume data.

## Build Images

Run from the server after `git pull`:

```bash
tutor images build openedx
tutor images build mfe
```

If Tutor config changed, run:

```bash
tutor config save
```

Keep the PostgreSQL Tutor plugin/config from `TutorOpenEdxPlugin.md` if that environment uses it.

## Production Start Commands

For Kubernetes/Tutor production environments, start or check services with:

```bash
tutor k8s start
kubectl get pods -n <namespace>
```

If only app pods need refresh after new images are pushed, delete Open edX pods and let Kubernetes recreate them:

```bash
kubectl delete pod -n <namespace> <lms-pod>
kubectl delete pod -n <namespace> <cms-pod>
kubectl delete pod -n <namespace> <worker-pod>
kubectl delete pod -n <namespace> <mfe-pod>
```

For logs:

```bash
kubectl logs -n <namespace> <lms-pod> --tail=100
kubectl logs -n <namespace> <cms-pod> --tail=100
```

For production migrations check:

```bash
tutor k8s exec lms -- ./manage.py lms migrate --check
tutor k8s exec cms -- ./manage.py cms migrate --check
```

Run real migrations only when the release includes migrations and backup/rollback is clear.

## Tag and Push

Use real registry/image names from the server.

Lab:

```bash
docker tag <local-openedx-image> <registry>/<openedx-image>:dev
docker tag <local-mfe-image> <registry>/<mfe-image>:dev
docker push <registry>/<openedx-image>:dev
docker push <registry>/<mfe-image>:dev
```

QA:

```bash
docker tag <local-openedx-image> <registry>/<openedx-image>:qa
docker tag <local-mfe-image> <registry>/<mfe-image>:qa
docker push <registry>/<openedx-image>:qa
docker push <registry>/<mfe-image>:qa
```

Production:

```bash
docker tag <local-openedx-image> <registry>/<openedx-image>:<release-tag>
docker tag <local-mfe-image> <registry>/<mfe-image>:<release-tag>
docker push <registry>/<openedx-image>:<release-tag>
docker push <registry>/<mfe-image>:<release-tag>

docker tag <registry>/<openedx-image>:<release-tag> <registry>/<openedx-image>:latest
docker tag <registry>/<mfe-image>:<release-tag> <registry>/<mfe-image>:latest
docker push <registry>/<openedx-image>:latest
docker push <registry>/<mfe-image>:latest
```

## Restart Pods

After image push, delete Open edX pods so Kubernetes creates new pods with the new image.

```bash
kubectl get pods -n <namespace>
kubectl delete pod -n <namespace> <lms-pod>
kubectl delete pod -n <namespace> <cms-pod>
kubectl delete pod -n <namespace> <worker-pod>
kubectl delete pod -n <namespace> <mfe-pod>
kubectl get pods -n <namespace>
```

Delete only Open edX app pods. Do not delete Postgres, Mongo, Redis, Elasticsearch, or storage pods.

If labels are known, label delete is also OK:

```bash
kubectl delete pod -n <namespace> -l <openedx-label>
kubectl delete pod -n <namespace> -l <mfe-label>
```

## Check After Deploy

```bash
kubectl get pods -n <namespace>
kubectl logs -n <namespace> <lms-pod> --tail=100
kubectl logs -n <namespace> <cms-pod> --tail=100
```

Smoke test:

- LMS opens.
- CMS/Studio opens.
- Networked login redirect works.
- Course list/detail works.
- Add lesson/edit lesson works.
- Publish works.
- Enroll/start/resume works.
- Student overview, scoreboard, and grading work if changed.

## Production Simple Checklist

- Deploy only reviewed release commit/tag.
- Push generated release tag first.
- Also tag same production image as `latest`.
- Know rollback image tag before deleting pods.
- After pods restart, check logs and smoke test main flows.

## If New Code Does Not Show

- Check pushed image tag.
- Check Kubernetes deployment image tag.
- Check image pull policy.
- Check pod image digest.
- Delete Open edX pod again only after confirming correct image was pushed.
